<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.VIBRATE" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />

    <application
        android:allowBackup="true"
        android:icon="@drawable/ic_launcher"
        android:label="NekoCalc"
        android:roundIcon="@mipmap/ic_launcher_round"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback="true"
        android:theme="@style/LaunchTheme">
        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:configChanges="orientation|keyboardHidden|keyboard|screenSize|smallestScreenSize|locale|layoutDirection|fontScale|screenLayout|density|uiMode"
            android:exported="true"
            android:hardwareAccelerated="true"
            android:launchMode="singleTop"
            android:screenOrientation="portrait"
            android:theme="@style/LaunchTheme"
            android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize">
            <!--
              中文：⚠️ 只写 `screenOrientation` 是**不够的**，因为 `targetSdk = 36`（跟随
                    `flutter.targetSdkVersion`，Flutter 3.44 解析为 36）。**Android 16 起，以 API 36
                    为目标的应用在最小宽度 ≥ 600dp 的屏幕上会被系统忽略方向限制**——属性写了也照样转。
                    Android 官方给的退出开关就是下面这个 property：声明它是"我们要保持不可调整大小"，
                    系统才恢复旧行为。
                    ⇒ 两个一起写才是「禁止屏幕旋转」；少一个，平板/折叠屏上就会转。
                    ⚠️ 应用的界面**没有横屏布局**（`lib/` 里 `isLandscape` / `OrientationBuilder` /
                    `MediaQuery.orientationOf` 各 **0** 处），所以锁竖屏不会留下任何死代码。
              English: ⚠️ `screenOrientation` **alone is not enough**, because `targetSdk = 36` (it follows
                    `flutter.targetSdkVersion`, which Flutter 3.44 resolves to 36). **From Android 16, an
                    app targeting API 36 has its orientation restriction ignored by the system on screens
                    with smallest width ≥ 600dp** — the attribute is simply not applied. Android's
                    documented opt-out is the property below: by declaring it the app asks to stay
                    non-resizable, and the system restores the old behaviour.
                    ⇒ Both lines together are "no screen rotation"; either alone and a tablet or foldable
                    will still rotate.
                    ⚠️ The UI has **no landscape layout at all** (`lib/` has **0** occurrences each of
                    `isLandscape`, `OrientationBuilder` and `MediaQuery.orientationOf`), so locking to
                    portrait leaves no dead code behind.
                    ⚠️ **This opt-out has an expiry date, and losing it would be silent.** Android's
                    behaviour-changes page (checked 2026-10-10) states the opt-out **no longer applies when
                    targeting API level 37** — from there the restrictions are ignored on `sw600dp` and up
                    regardless. So **the day `flutter.targetSdkVersion` becomes 37, this file silently stops
                    locking tablets and foldables**; a phone is unaffected either way (`sw < 600dp` is an
                    explicit exception, which is also why the attribute alone is enough on phones). The
                    durable answer at that point is a real large-screen layout, not another flag.
            -->
            <property
                android:name="android.window.PROPERTY_COMPAT_ALLOW_RESTRICTED_RESIZABILITY"
                android:value="true" />
            <meta-data
                android:name="io.flutter.embedding.android.NormalTheme"
                android:resource="@style/NormalTheme" />
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
        <meta-data
            android:name="flutterEmbedding"
            android:value="2" />
    </application>
</manifest>
